From: TDVP <tdvp@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tdvp: link libdl for runtime panel-plugin loading

wf-panel-pi discovers its panel modules with dlopen() and dlsym().  On this
RISC-V toolchain libdl is not pulled in transitively, so the final panel
executable fails to link.  Declare the direct dependency in Meson rather than
relying on a Buildroot-specific linker flag.

Signed-off-by: TDVP <tdvp@example.invalid>
---
 src/panel/meson.build | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panel/meson.build b/src/panel/meson.build
index 620fc03..d695073 100644
--- a/src/panel/meson.build
+++ b/src/panel/meson.build
@@ -34,7 +34,8 @@ udev = dependency('libudev')
 input = dependency('libinput')
 evdev = dependency('libevdev')
 libxml2 = dependency('libxml-2.0')
-panel_deps = [ gtklayershell, udev, input, evdev, libxml2 ]
+libdl = meson.get_compiler('cpp').find_library('dl', required: true)
+panel_deps = [ gtklayershell, udev, input, evdev, libxml2, libdl ]
 
 executable('wf-panel-pi', panel_sources + util_sources + config_sources,
         dependencies: deps + panel_deps,
